repository-code: 'https://github.com/zhakansadykov/ADRON-55'
abstract: >-
  An open, scripted reconstruction pipeline for the ADRON-55
  ionization calorimeter at the Tien Shan high-altitude cosmic-ray
  station (3340 m a.s.l., Kazakhstan). The pipeline decodes the raw
  per-section detector format, assembles the overlapping chamber
  sections into a position measurement, applies a data-driven
  channel-to-position calibration and track-based plane alignment,
  performs an integrity and good-run selection, finds clusters and
  projection tracks with a road search confined to the hadron block,
  and fits three-dimensional directions with a weighted
  least-squares line. Diagnostic scripts reproduce every calibration
  and every figure of the accompanying paper from the raw data.
keywords:
  - cosmic rays
  - extensive air showers
  - ionization calorimeter
  - event reconstruction
  - detector calibration
  - track-based alignment
  - reproducibility
